{
  "about": [
    "The strip pictures of the console screens, which tools/make_strips.py builds. Each console has six, listed from left to right.",
    "system and file: a screenshot in roms/<system>/snap/ of a RetroPie card. or: the same game's picture from libretro-thumbnails, with its own thumbnails, file and focus, for a card without that screenshot.",
    "thumbnails and file: a picture from the Named_Snaps folder of that libretro-thumbnails repository on GitHub, or from the folder in folder (Named_Titles for a title screen).",
    "focus: the centre of the game's most recognizable part, as a share of the screenshot's width.",
    "rows: the top and bottom of the part to use, as shares of the screenshot's height, to leave out black bars and subtitles.",
    "3d: true for 3D graphics, which grow with Lanczos resampling in place of Scale2x.",
    "bright: a factor that lightens a dark screenshot.",
    "A console missing here shows screenshots of its own games, chosen by the strips patterns in consoles.json."
  ],
